# Round 18, C1-16 (follows). L §4.3: "A read through a def that states its own at needs none, unless that at itself
# reads something law-dated, which is read at the line's law date (at e, below)"; "the reads inside e are made at the
# law date of the read that asks for the def (its reader's, or the ask's law)". q reads surprise_dom at 2026-03-01
# (10), so fee at 2026-03-10 (5); q2 at 2026-08-01 (20), so fee at 2026-03-20 (7). L4_3_at_reads_lawdated_no_law: the
# line without law is LOAD-LAWDATE.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input surprise_dom: int
input fee: money PLN
def charged[m in months]: money PLN = fee at day_of(m, surprise_dom)
version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..2026-06-30
  known 2025-12-01
  surprise_dom = 10
version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026-07-01..
  known 2025-12-01
  surprise_dom = 20
version f
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  fee = 5 governs 2026-01-01..2026-03-15
  fee = 7 governs 2026-03-16..
ask q: charged[2026-03] law 2026-03-01
ask q2: charged[2026-03] law 2026-08-01
=== expect
q: 5.00 PLN
  law date 2026-03-01, cut 2026-12-31
q2: 7.00 PLN
  law date 2026-08-01, cut 2026-12-31
